David Damerell <damerell@chiark.greenend.org.uk> writes:

> You can, but that would be daft because you are extremely unlikely
> to find the four to seven items you want most in a shop, and you
> then have to get them out from under the feet of the shopkeeper.

Well, the stealing part is trivial. I recently had a game where I
found shops with a bag of holding, a magic marker, a cloak of magic
resistance, a magic whistle, speed boots, and gauntlets of power from
shops in three adjacent early levels (pre-Oracle). It is not exactly
rare to find an early armour shop with two or three ascension kit
items.

And speaking about shop luck, I don't think anyone can top my monk who
found a wand shop in dungeon level 2 with *TWO* wands of wishing. Not
one, but two. I was 100% absolutely certain that I would ascend that
one but unfortunately too long time had passed from my last monk
ascension that I once again underestimated Master Kaen (what do you
mean? 150 HP, -26 AC, magic resistance, speed boots, and an amulet of
life saving not enough to bash him in fair combat? Don't be
ridiculous. *splat*)

> The idea is not to make the average game harder up until the Castle. In
> the average game, you don't _find_ an early WoW. The idea is to eliminate
> the extreme outlying case, where the early and middle games are really
> disproportionately easy.

Do you also propose to eliminate the extreme outlying cases to the
other direction? You know, the cases where the early and middle games
are absolutely impossible, like the ones where you find the proverbial
gnome with a wand of death? Or the cases like what happened to my last
priest who was happily wandering in pre-Oracle Dungeons of Doom when a
blast of fire came from a dark corridor, hit him, burned his only
scroll of teleportation and boiled a potion of extra healing, leaving
him no choice but to die on the next turn without ever seeing the
assailant? [A later explorer found a hell hound pup from the same
level, probably a potion of polymorph (too early for traps) though I
don't remember ever seeing the "chugging sound" message]. If you are
hell-bent on removing the easy outliers, why not also these?

> It is not bashing people to observe that ascension is much easier if you
> get an early WoW. That's a plain, factual observation.

And it is also a plain, factual observation that a character who finds
speed boots and a bag of holding on dungeon level 2 has much easier
time to ascend than one who doesn't.

As for limiting Wand of Wishing charges, I don't see a point for it.
Finding an early one makes an ascension 90% certain? So what. If you
find that such a break of luck makes the game uninteresting, then
escape the dungeon and start a new one.

